# PROJECT CONTEXT — read before doing anything

What this is: «Агро-Севооборот» (Agro-Rotation), our NASA Space Apps 2026 project for the challenge
"Field Shift: Adapting Farms with NASA Data". It is a decision-support web app for farmers and agronomists in
Northern Kazakhstan (Akmola, Kostanay, North Kazakhstan oblasts), where fields are dominated by spring wheat
grown year after year, with long periods of bare soil and a history of severe wind erosion.

What it does: a farmer creates an account, draws a field on the map, and sees long-term NASA data for that
field (rainfall and temperature from NASA POWER, vegetation NDVI from MODIS, soil moisture from SMAP, soil
properties from SoilGrids). The app rates the season's risks and compares 2–4 crop rotations on soil, water,
income and risk over 3–5 years, with economics, a drought stress test and an explanation for every score.
It exports PDF and Excel reports in Russian, Kazakh and English. There is an offline demo at /demo with two
real fields (Shortandy, Akmola; Kostanay).

What it is used for: helping farmers explore rotations that protect soil and cope with drought. It is a
support tool, not an oracle: every number shows its source, data type (observation / reanalysis / model),
resolution and period, and anything unverified is marked "requires checking". The farmer decides.

What we are adding this weekend: the "Bare Soil Clock", which shows month by month when a field is bare AND
windy AND dry (erosion exposure) and when a cover crop could fit; bare-soil numbers in the rotation planner;
live status of the GPM and Landsat data sources; and a Telegram bot entry point. My teammate builds the
backend in Claude Code at the same time. I build ONLY the frontend.

Stack: React 18 + TypeScript strict + Vite + Tailwind + react-leaflet + recharts + i18next (ru/kk/en).
Key files: frontend/src/pages/app/FieldWorkspace.tsx (field tabs), frontend/src/components/workspace/*
(one component per tab), frontend/src/components/ui/ui.tsx (Loading, ErrorBox, EmptyState, Notice,
KindBadge, LevelBadge, SectionTitle, Tabs), frontend/src/components/charts/ChartFrame.tsx (chart wrapper
with caption and data table), frontend/src/components/workspace/SourceList.tsx, frontend/src/lib/async.ts
(useAsync), frontend/src/lib/colors.ts (RAMPS), frontend/src/api/client.ts and api/types.ts,
frontend/src/locales/{ru,kk,en}.json.

## Hard rules

1. Edit only frontend/. Never edit backend/, scripts/ or docs/contracts/. If you need a new API field,
   write it in docs/contracts/REQUESTS.md instead.
2. The API contract is docs/contracts/bare_soil.example.json. Do not change its shape.
3. Reuse existing components and patterns; copy how Monitoring.tsx and RiskTab.tsx are built
   (useAsync, background-job polling, ChartFrame with a table under each chart, SourceList).
4. Every chart shows source, data type, resolution and period, and has a data table. Colour is never the
   only carrier of meaning. Unverified values show a "requires checking" badge.
5. Nothing may be demo-only: new fields drawn by users must get the same features with live data.
6. Every UI string goes into ru.json, kk.json and en.json with identical keys and placeholders. List any
   Kazakh strings you wrote at the end of your answer so a native speaker can review them.
7. Must work at 390 px width with no horizontal scroll, and with the keyboard.
8. Before finishing: run `make build` (TypeScript strict) and fix all errors. Tell me which files you changed.

